> On Mon, Dec 22, 2003 at 04:24:21PM +0100, Romain Guerout wrote:
> >
> > I have a Miata PWS 500au running both
> > Tru64 v5.1 with X11 and
> > RedHat Linux 7.2 with Xfree v 4.3.0.
> >
> > I want to invest in another graphic card
> > What I want for sure is a resolution of 1280x1024
> > with 16 millions colors.
> >
> > Can someone give me any hints about a graphic card
> > fulfilling these requirements compatible with both X11 and Xfree 4.3.0
>
> Two recent cards that come to mind are:
>
> 1. 3DLabs Oxygen VX1 - 32MB of memory and much faster than Permedia 2
cards
>
>    Use under Tru64 requires either 5.1A or 4.0F-5.1 with a patch.
>
> 2. ATI Radeon 7500 - 64MB of memory and capable of 3D under X11 or XFree86
>
>    Use under Tru64 requires 5.1B (and for 3D, an Open3D license)
>
> Both the above work nicely with the XFree86 4.1.0 found in RH 7.2 for
Alpha,
> and stock 4.3.0.
>
> Good luck.
>
