>
> I eBayed an XP1000 last week, built it up with a VX1 card and 1 G of RAM and
> loaded RH 7.2 from ISOs downloaded about 12/02.  The install went very well,
> without any of the CDrom BS i'm used to with the Miatas.  But...
>
> The machine will boot right up to where the X starts up.  The screen goes
> black and stays that way, and no combination of keys I've tried can get back
> to text mode. Ctrl-Alt_Del gets you out OK to a reboot and more of the same.
>
> The only way I've found to get into the machine is to boot single user, then
> init 3, then startx, which brings up the full glory of KDE.  This works for
> root only, if I try it in the user accounts i get a message "insufficient
> permission" WRT the Xserver.

First, change the default runlevel from 5 to 3:  Boot to
single user mode (or rescue mode, or something).  Edit
file /etc/inittab.  Find the line containing 'initdefault'
(without the quote marks).  Change the '5' to '3'.  Reboot.

>From there, you have a couple of ways to configure X.  One
way is XConfigurator, supplied with RHL 7.2 but not with
later versions.  Another is 'XFree86 -configure' (without
the quote marks).  Whenever you change graphics cards or
monitors, you should usually adjust or recreate the config
file.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net



